<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Prince of Wales Island</h1><p class="st-meta">1786 CE – 1826 CE · capital George Town</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">British East India Company settlement on Penang, founded by Francis Light, the first British base on the Strait of Malacca.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Seeking a naval and trading base on the eastern side of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-bengal">Bay of Bengal</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> trader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-light">Francis Light</a> negotiated with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kedah-sultanate">Kedah</a>, who hoped for protection against Siam. Light landed on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penang">Penang</a> in August 1786, renamed it <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a> Island and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-town-penang">George Town</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The settlement was a free port that drew Chinese, Indian, Malay, Acehnese and Eurasian traders, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spice-trade">spices</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepper">pepper</a> were planted. In 1800 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> added the mainland strip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/province-wellesley">Province Wellesley</a>. In 1805 it was raised to the status of a presidency of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/british-raj">British India</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stamford-raffles">Thomas Stamford Raffles</a> serving as assistant secretary.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Hopes of a naval dockyard faded and the rise of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/singapore">Singapore</a> overshadowed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penang">Penang</a>. In 1826 it was merged with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a> to form the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/straits-settlements">Straits Settlements</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-town-penang">George Town</a> later became the capital of the Malaysian state of Penang.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1786 CE – 1826 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Maritime Southeast Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:95.24%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1786 CE – 1826 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>George Town</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Francis Light</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam, Chinese folk religion, Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Malay, English, Hokkien</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/malaysia">Malaysia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Penang, Penang (British)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1806&amp;focus=prince-of-wales-island" aria-label="Prince of Wales Island on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7461 1975 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Prince of Wales Island lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7781 2231L4997 651M7781 2231L7364 1601M7781 2231L7883 2385"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4997 651h0M7364 1601h0M7883 2385h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7781 2231h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7781 2231h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks George Town. <a href="/atlas?year=1806&amp;focus=prince-of-wales-island">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
